course: dictionary
lesson: 4025
title: Gathering: one word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gathering can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a gathering is a group of people who meet together. As a verb, to gather means to collect things together. «Our family gathering was at Granny's house on Sunday.» Here the words family and house tell you it is a group of people meeting.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «She was gathering shells on the beach.» Shells are things you can collect, so gathering means collecting. Check by swapping in your meaning: "She was collecting shells on the beach" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Weather can be a clue too. «Dark clouds are gathering over the hill.» The clouds are coming together, so a storm may be on its way. Look at the nearby words, such as clouds, to decide which meaning fits.
fact: A gathering is a group of people who meet together, often for a special reason.
fact: Gathering can also mean collecting things together, like food or information.
fact: «A wake is a gathering after a funeral where people eat, drink and share stories.» Laughing there does not mean nobody is sad.
fact: «Karakia are Māori chants or prayers, often used to open gatherings in New Zealand.»
fact: «Many Hindu families hold prayers and gatherings for about thirteen days after a death.» Hindus believe the soul moves on to a new life.
exercise: «Our family gathering was at Granny's house on Sunday.» What is a gathering here? | A storm | A type of cloth | A pile of leaves | *A group of people who meet together
exercise: «She was gathering shells on the beach.» What is she doing? | Breaking the shells | Hiding from the waves | *Collecting shells together | Painting the sand
exercise: «Dark clouds are gathering over the hill.» What might happen next? | The sun will shine brightly | The hill will disappear | *A storm may be on its way | The clouds will start to sing
test: «Many Hindu families hold prayers and gatherings for about thirteen days after a death.» What does gatherings mean here? | Loud music | Strong winds | Hiding places | *Groups of people meeting together
test: Mum says, «Please gather the toys and put them in the box.» What should you do? | *Pick them up and put them in one place | Ignore them | Break them | Paint them red
exam: Ella says «gathering» always means a school test. Is she right? | Yes, a gathering is always a test | No, because gatherings only happen in the rain | Yes, but only in Cork | *No, a gathering is a group of people meeting together, or collecting things
